Step 0: go to https://physionet.org/content/eegmmidb/1.0.0/S001/#files-panel to download the ZIP file: eeg-motor-movementimagery-dataset-1.0.0.zip. 
Then use the file 
  Step0_preprocessingData.ipynb 
to pre-process and z-scoring the data and save as npy files.



Step 1: train the pretrain universal VAE by running:

bash -lc 'export CUBLAS_WORKSPACE_CONFIG=:4096:8; export PYTHONHASHSEED=0; export OMP_NUM_THREADS=1; export MKL_NUM_THREADS=1; \
> python Step01_universalVAE_subjsplit70_10_29_win9_R03to14_centeraware.py \
>   --data-dir EEGMI_numpy \
>   --output checkpoints_vae_261028001/vae_universal_subjsplit70_10_29_win9_R03to14_hd512_ld8_beta3e-04_split123_sample123_torch123_ep100.pth \
>   --train-n 70 --val-n 10 --test-n 29 \
>   --split-seed 123 --sample-seed 123 --torch-seed 123 \
>   --window-points 9 --stride-points 1 \
>   --downsample-factor-train 30 --downsample-factor-eval 30 \
>   --hidden-dim 512 --latent-dim 8 \
>   --beta 3e-4 --huber-delta 1.0 --center-weight 5.0 \
>   --epochs 100 --batch-size 512 --lr 1e-3 \
>   --device cuda'

If it succeeds in running, it should be like:
